//! The `math-depth` property describes a notion of _depth_ for each element of a mathematical
//! formula, with respect to the top-level container of that formula. This is used to scale the
//! computed value of the
//! [font-size](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-size) of
//! elements when `font-size: math` is applied.
//!
//! Initial: 0. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: auto-add | add(<integer>) | <integer>
//!
//! Specification: https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#propdef-math-depth
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/math-depth
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

